{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>They have dealt corruptly with Him, not His children, their blemish. They have dealt corruptly with Him</b> — HaShem dealt corruptly with them, that they were not His children. As Hoshea said: 'You are not My people.' And your sins turned away these who were called <b>not His children.</b> Another interpretation: if He dealt corruptly and exacted retribution from the children of men — not to Him does the matter apply, as it is written: 'for He does not afflict from His heart, and He grieves the children of a man.'" "<b>His children, their blemish.</b> A parable: that their corruption is a blemish in them — meaning, from them the corruption comes."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:59.891814383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}